    "1": {
      "note": "Sentence-final particles sit at the very end of a sentence and add emotional or grammatical flavour without changing the literal meaning. They're what makes Cantonese sound natural — speech without them feels flat and robotic. <strong>Tone matters a lot</strong>: <em>laa1</em> (softening) and <em>laa3</em> (now / completion) are different particles, not variants. Don't try to translate each one literally — instead, learn the feeling each adds: certainty, surprise, gentleness, limitation, or inviting agreement.",
